# The rules no refused program of tests/ states, one line each: the rule's
# phrase, a tab, its kind, a tab, why. tests/rules-covered reads this
# file: every rule of the specification's table (`runtests --rules`) has a
# fixture whose `-- expect:` header names it, or a line here, never both.
# `unreachable`: no source program reaches the refusal. `elsewhere`:
# another test reaches it. `owed`: a source program reaches it; its fixture
# is written when a build shows one.
compiled module	unreachable	raised when the compiled module the frontend reads lacks a definition or a constructor it names (lookupDef in Translate/Closed.idr, instanceKey in Translate/Keys.idr, Translate/Types.idr, Translate/Cases.idr), which no module Idris checked lacks
runtime	unreachable	raised by the driver when the runtime object it links lacks a member (foreign/idr/lib/Driver/ReadRuntime.cpp): the toolchain's object, not a program
data type	unreachable	raised for a data type whose constructors Idris does not record, an [external] type (Translate/Types.idr); a value of one that is no runtime handle comes only from %foreign, refused as escape hatch first (Frontend/Profile.idr)
definition	unreachable	raised for a reached definition that is not pattern matching (Translate/Programs.idr); Idris elaborates every definition of a source as one, and the reach check refuses or hooks the others, primitives, %extern, %foreign and holes, before translation (Frontend/Profile.idr)
string primitive	unreachable	raised for a literal match on a constant that is no literal, a primitive type or the world (Translate/Cases.idr); a match on a type value is a type in a runtime position, refused as type, and user code has no world to match
runtime closure	owed	raised where a closure's or an implementation's member set, or its use types, are ones no analysis bounds: a function computed at run time applied inside a settled term, a form whose type its body does not give, a value an implementation closes over computed inside another of its own (Translate/Terms.idr), an implementation's field no compile-time reduction reaches (Translate/Cases.idr); a run-time choice among implementations the program fixes, which once reached it, now compiles, so which source program still reaches a site is for a build to show
match	owed	raised for a match on an erased value between several alternatives (Translate/Cases.idr); a literal match Idris proved complete compiles, its last alternative standing in for the default
